    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the \"lessons learned\" angle, but I'm worried that if we just talk about what we learned, it'll look like we failed. The GEF is incredibly competitive. They want to see winners. \n\nCan we go a bit further with the framing? Like, instead of focusing on the 5% number, can we talk about the \"foundational progress\" or \"established baseline\" we created? I need something that makes the 5% look like a win rather than a miss. How can we write this so they see us as a proven success story?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
